  "new_v0_5_claims": [
    "the DFT-conjugated canonical width projector has an exact 0/1 mask indexed by divisors of T and is idempotent",
    "canonical Reynolds projectors commute and compose by lcm on divisor widths",
    "the range of the lcm projector is exactly the intersection of the two projector ranges",
    "finite products of canonical Reynolds projectors collapse to the projector at the finite lcm, with exact finite range-intersection equality",
    "the cyclic subgroup embedding Z/gZ -> Z/TZ is injective for g|T, and the restricted Fourier character is trivial exactly on frequencies whose representatives are divisible by g",
    "the literal uniform subgroup Reynolds average diagonalizes under the Mathlib DFT to the same exact 0/1 width mask and equals the DFT-conjugated Reynolds projector",
    "for positive raw radices m,n, the canonical reduction g_m=gcd(T,m) satisfies lcm(g_m,g_n)=gcd(T,lcm(m,n)), hence P_m P_n=P_lcm(m,n) and Range(P_m) \u2229 Range(P_n)=Range(P_lcm(m,n))",
    "the same raw-radix lcm composition and range-intersection laws hold for finite positive radix lists",
    "affine polynomial substitution X -> mX+r is a complex-linear equivalence for m>0 and its forward map is exactly the retained baseline affineSubst",
    "for the explicitly defined projector-factorized affine section normal form, an explicit decoder satisfies AB=P_gcd(T,m), ABA=A, and BAB=B",
    "frequency shells labeled by gcd(T,k) reproduce the certified width coordinates, decompose the DFT width mask into primitive shells, and agree exactly with the saved M\u00f6bius shell formula",
    "the resulting DFT primitive-shell projectors are idempotent and pairwise orthogonal"
  ],
  "explicit_boundaries": [
    "Bell generalized Cobham theorem remains an external input to the earlier two-radix collapse-to-cyclotomic step and is not formalized here",
    "the integral base-independent normal form remains false in the naive form; the square-sequence radix-prime obstruction is retained",
    "the package proves a product-coordinate algebra equivalence, not a separately constructed categorical tensor-product equivalence of local algebras",
    "the affine generalized-inverse theorems apply to the explicitly defined projector-factorized affine section normal form; this release does not identify that normal form with any stronger unsaved root-aggregation section operator",
    "the exact characteristic-zero rank/nullity formula from the continuation plan is not formalized in v0.5.0 and remains open",
    "the raw-radix lcm laws are proved in the positive-radix regime; zero radices are not silently folded into the section semigroup",
    "the DFT/Reynolds results are finite complex residue-profile theorems; they do not establish a base-independent integral lattice normal form",
    "Lean verification of these statements does not by itself establish literature novelty or priority"
  ],
  "external_inputs": [
    {
      "name": "Bell generalized Cobham theorem",
      "status": "external / not formalized",
      "use_boundary": "may only enter downstream as an explicit hypothesis/interface"
    }
  ],
  "open_next": [
    "exact characteristic-zero rank/nullity law for degree-d quasi-polynomial profiles, with the positive-characteristic obstruction isolated",
    "a precise Bell-conclusion interface, keeping Bell external, followed by the uniform all-radix common-hull theorem",
    "active-shell/minimal-hull sharpening after the Bell interface",
    "localized integral common-lattice theory retaining Smith/Fitting/radix-local defects rather than reviving naive integral base-independence"
  ],
